{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedSlide","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedSlide","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cup_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cup_left","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedSlide.lean#L100-L110","doc":"**A strand slides across a cup**, mirror image of `braiding_slide_cup_right`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cup_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cup_right","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedSlide.lean#L86-L98","doc":"**A strand slides across a cup**, braiding past each leg in turn.\n\nThe cup-shaped dual of `braiding_slide_cap_right`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cap_right_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cap_right_inv","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedSlide.lean#L70-L84","doc":"**The inverse form of `braiding_slide_cap_right`** — the one an assembly actually uses.\n\nRead left to right: a strand `W` that crosses only the *second* leg `B` before the cap can still be\npushed off, but it leaves behind an **inverse** braiding past the first leg `A`.  That leftover is\nwhere a monodromy comes from: apply this twice, once for each leg of a dual pair, and the two\nleftovers compose to a double braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cap_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cap_left","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedSlide.lean#L57-L68","doc":"**A strand slides across a cap**, mirror image of `braiding_slide_cap_right`.\n\n`W` starts to the right of `A ⊗ B` and ends to its left. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cap_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.braiding_slide_cap_right","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedSlide.lean#L44-L55","doc":"**A strand slides across a cap**, braiding past each leg in turn.\n\n`W` starts to the left of `A ⊗ B` and ends to its right. ","signatureChunk":0}]}